Kount — a "New collection…" entry in the Add item dialog's Collections list (plan claim-and-sso item 1, D10).

The admin console's add form lists "New collection…" last in its Collections field. Picking it opens the usual collection
dialog (A1's External ID included) with the name prefilled from the item; on Save the new collection is added to the
form's list and selected beside what was already selected. The form only takes an optional `newCollection` from its config:
only the admin console's config service gives one, and only for someone who can create collections, so every other client
of the shared form is unchanged. The Saved result is the server's response, whose name is ciphertext (docs/spike-2026-11.md
S1), so the provider re-reads the collection by id. Cut against the tree with A1 and P5 applied; applied in name order.

